quest title=The Heart of Ironreef
quest intro=A ruined mining camp on a jungle mountain. The Ironreef Mining Company struck rich iron here - then left in a hurry. Their notice board still stands on the beach.
step reach|camp|1|Land at the abandoned mining camp
step read|Company notice|1|Read the company's notice board
step open|Supply barrel|1|Raid the company's supply barrel by the campfire
step reach|shoulder|1|Climb the plank road up the cliff to the mountain's shoulder
step reach|irongate|1|Follow the shoulder to the Iron Gate mine
step kill|Warthog|2|Drive the two warthogs out of the dark along the rails
step read|Foreman's log|1|Read the foreman's log at the back of the mine
step open|Foreman's locker|1|Take the foreman's spare lamp from his locker
step reach|vines|1|Crawl into the Vine Crawl on the east flank
step open|Powder crate|1|Find the powder crate wedged behind the vines
step collect|story:charges|1|Take the first bundle of charges - the other is down the sea adit
step reach|hallmouth|1|Go round to the north flank, where the Bear Hall was blasted shut
step read|Rockfall|1|Read the foreman's warning on the rockfall
step pages||7|Try the rockfall - see what one charge won't do
step reach|drowned|1|Take a deep breath and dive into the Drowned Shaft
step open|Sunken powder box|1|Find the sunken powder box on the flooded floor of the adit
step collect|story:charges|2|Bring both blasting charges back to the rockfall
step pages||9|Wedge both charges into the rockfall and blow it open
step reach|bearhall|1|Enter the Bear Hall
step kill|Bear|1|Defeat Ironhide
step open|Company strongbox|1|Open the company's strongbox
step blueprint|Blueprint_TitaniumTools|1|Take the titanium tools plans from the company strongbox
quest done=Ironhide is dead and the strongbox is open: the Heart of Ironreef - a fist-sized lump of pure iron - and the blueprint the company kept from its miners are yours.
quest reward=MetalIngot*8;Nail*20;Bolt*6

# --- A Raft store on the north beach: the mining company's tally shop, still trading (Raft's goods, and plans the crew missed) --
store tallyshop at 8 54 ground

# Buried treasure (one of the story line's last islands): titanium ore on top of Raft's own treasure loot - the metal detector finds it, the shovel digs it
call treasure x=0 z=0 r=55 n=1 seed=8813
prop treasure8813 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*3
# DEEP 10-25: Davy Rees's pay, buried on the west tableland (his letter in the Bear Hall says where)
call treasure x=-60 z=-28 r=20 n=1 seed=32030 kind=0
prop treasure32030 treasure.loot=MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;Bolt*3

# --- ABYSS 10-26 (1-hour pass): the company's survey on the west tableland, its tallies, the plane and the ore boat ---
# A The company plane, down on the west tableland (h 10), its crate beside it
call ar_plane x=-72 z=-38 h=10.2 yaw=50 al=companyplane crate=companycrate
note companycrate Company plane's crate | The company plane's freight: survey pegs, rope and a box of bolts, flown in for the tableland survey and never unloaded.
loot companycrate Rope*3;Bolt*3;MetalIngot*2
call hw_zone x=-72 z=-30 al=planez id=companyplane r=6 msg="The company plane, down on the tableland. Its wing lies in the grass; the survey it brought was never finished."
# B The survey beacons (puzzle: all three lit shows the surveyor's cache); a beacon switches its neighbours too.
# Start: 1 and 2 lit; beacon 1, then beacon 2, lights them all.
call ab_lamp x=-100 z=-22 al=beacon1 nm="Survey beacon 1" grp="Survey beacons" on=1
call ab_lamp x=-88 z=-30 al=beacon2 nm="Survey beacon 2" grp="Survey beacons" on=1
call ab_lamp x=-62 z=-56 al=beacon3 nm="Survey beacon 3" grp="Survey beacons" on=0
prop beacon1 on.use=light|Survey beacon 2|toggle
prop beacon2 on.use=light|Survey beacon 1|toggle\nlight|Survey beacon 3|toggle
prop beacon3 on.use=light|Survey beacon 2|toggle
prop beacon1 on.alllit=show|surveycache\nmessage||All three survey beacons burn across the tableland. By the first, the surveyor's cache stands open.
call ab_hidden x=-94 z=-18 al=surveycache
note surveycache Surveyor's cache | The company surveyor's cache: his instruments, his pay and a sample of the best ore he found.
loot surveycache TitaniumOre*2;MetalIngot*3;TradeToken*2
# C The ore boat, run aground on the north beach, its crate beside it
call hw_wreck x=-10 z=96 h=2 yaw=200 obj=BoatStranded al=oreboat crate=oreboatcrate r=9
note oreboatcrate Ore boat's crate | The ore boat's last load, never shipped: iron and copper ingots under a tarpaulin.
loot oreboatcrate MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Rope*2
# D Company tallies: five brass tallies of the company's miners, lost about the island (a set: a secret)
call ab_piece x=68 z=8 al=ctally1 set="Company tallies" nm="Company tally 1"
call ab_piece x=-30 z=92 al=ctally2 set="Company tallies" nm="Company tally 2"
call ab_piece x=-58 z=-48 al=ctally3 set="Company tallies" nm="Company tally 3"
call ab_piece x=20 z=-92 al=ctally4 set="Company tallies" nm="Company tally 4"
call ab_piece x=60 z=58 al=ctally5 set="Company tallies" nm="Company tally 5"
prop ctally1 on.set=give||TitaniumIngot*1;MetalIngot*2\nmessage||All five company tallies. Every miner of Ironreef is accounted for.
# E Dr. Calder's field note, by the company's wagon in the camp
place Note_Paper caldernote3 at 79 -10 ground y=0.1 drop yaw=60
note caldernote3 Dr. Ruth Calder's field note | THE ABYSS EXPEDITION - FIELD NOTE 3\n\nIronreef. The company dug for iron and found the sea under the mountain instead. Their foreman's log talks of a pump store in a drowned city - Meridian - and a key they never used.\n\nThe ore here is good, but it is not what we came for. The soundings all point the same way: deeper, and east.\n\nWe take the company's key and go on.\n- R. C.
# F The scaffold run on the east beach (a hop course on its own pad)
# --- JUMP COURSE ir (Abyss pass 10-26): kz-style hop course of floor slabs on its own pad (the bs course, turned) ---
# JUMP ir pad=2.5 at=88 26
push at 88 26
clear at 0 0 r=17 all
brush flatten at 0 0 r=14 s=20 frames=300 h=2.5
brush smooth at 0 0 r=18 s=4 frames=40
brush flatten at 0 0 r=12 s=20 frames=300 h=2.5
brush auto at 0 0 r=18 s=10 frames=25
clear at 0 0 r=18
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at 5.64 -0.10 h=3.10
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at 5.64 -2.92 h=3.60
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at 5.64 -5.93 h=4.00
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at 3.03 -5.93 h=4.90
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -1.21 -5.93 h=5.40 sx=3 sz=0.3
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -5.64 -5.93 h=6.20
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -5.64 -3.02 h=7.10
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -5.64 -0.40 h=6.10
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -5.64 2.41 h=7.05
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -5.64 5.12 h=8.00
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -2.02 5.12 h=8.90 sx=2 sz=2
# JUMP from 11
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at -2.02 -1.30 h=9.20 sx=2 sz=2
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jpir at 3.21 -1.30 h=9.50
# JUMP end
# (each slab on one solid column of its own footprint, from under the pad up to the slab)
# (the first slab rests on the pad itself: no column)
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at 5.64 -2.92 h=2.918 sy=1.493
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at 5.64 -5.93 h=3.318 sy=2.079
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at 3.03 -5.93 h=4.218 sy=3.399
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -1.21 -5.93 h=4.718 sy=4.132 sx=3 sz=0.3
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -5.64 -5.93 h=5.518 sy=5.305
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -5.64 -3.02 h=6.418 sy=6.625
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -5.64 -0.40 h=5.418 sy=5.158
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -5.64 2.41 h=6.368 sy=6.551
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -5.64 5.12 h=7.318 sy=7.944
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -2.02 5.12 h=8.218 sy=9.264 sx=2 sz=2
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at -2.02 -1.30 h=8.518 sy=9.704 sx=2 sz=2
place Block_Foundation_Tier3 jppir at 3.21 -1.30 h=8.818 sy=10.144
prop jpir tint.color=#6b5a48
prop jpir tint.amount=0.35
prop jppir tint.color=#6b5a48
prop jppir tint.amount=0.35
place Loot_Chest jcir at -2.02 5.12 h=8.90 sit yaw=0
note jcir Scaffold perch | The miners raced up the scaffold on pay day; the winner sat up here and watched the ore boats come in.
loot jcir Plank*6;Rope*3;MetalIngot*1
prop jcir loot.refill=0
place Loot_ChestSmall jbir at 3.21 -1.30 h=9.50 sit yaw=0
note jbir Scaffold run prize | A tin wedged on the last scaffold post: a miner's pay-day winnings.
loot jbir MetalIngot*2;CopperIngot*2;TitaniumIngot*1
prop jbir loot.refill=0
place Zone_Trigger jyir at 3.21 -1.30 h=10.50
prop jyir zone.id=jump_ir_finale
prop jyir zone.radius=1.8
prop jyir zone.repeat=never
prop jyir zone.message=The top of the scaffold run - a tin is wedged on the last post.
pop
# --- end of jump course ir ---

# (generator stones left in the air by the shaping - taken out, 10-25)
clear at 23.03 -9.93 r=1.5 only=BigBoulder1_Low
clear at 90.21 -40.6 r=1.5 only=BigBoulder2_Low
clear at -63.18 -16.08 r=1 only=SmallBoulder2
clear at -25.46 -44.26 r=1.5 only=BigBoulder2_Low
clear at 8.76 12.65 r=1 only=SmallBoulder4
clear at 27.53 -30.38 r=1 only=SmallBoulder4
clear at -20.88 5.62 r=1 only=SmallBoulder3
clear at 83.05 -57.57 r=1.5 only=BigBoulder2_Low
save Ironreef Caverns
